        {
          "_key": "y4p7dg61c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When working with artificial intelligence (AI) technology, one term you'll encounter frequently is the 'AI token.' But what exactly is an AI token, and why does it matter for your projects? In this article, we'll delve into the basics of AI tokens, covering everything from token counting to pricing and usage management. By the end of this guide, you'll have a solid understanding of how AI tokens work and be able to apply this knowledge in your own projects."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "w2qxsnus",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "w2qxsnusc",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What is an AI Token?"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k3jm5a9b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "k3jm5a9bc",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "An AI token is the unit of measurement for language models to process text. It's a fundamental concept that underlies how many AI applications work, from chatbots and virtual assistants to language translation services."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "hmkofp1g",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "hmkofp1gc",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In essence, an AI token represents a single piece of information that the model can understand and process. This could be a word, a character, or even a subword (a smaller unit of text that's part of a larger word)."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "m61f94mo",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "m61f94moc",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Token Counts vs Word/Character Count"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "bfh8gi5b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "bfh8gi5bc",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "One common misconception about AI tokens is that they're always equal to the number of words or characters in a piece of text. However, this isn't necessarily true."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "z90r7g87",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "z90r7g87c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Token counting is a complex process that takes into account the specific language model being used and its requirements for processing text. In some cases, a single word might be counted as multiple tokens, while in others, a character might be split across multiple tokens."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
